<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/Q86SK9">
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Stearoyl-CoA desaturase 5</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_Q86SK9" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_SCD5_identity" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SCD5_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Acyl-CoA-desaturase 4</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Stearoyl-CoA 9-desaturase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">HSCD5</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.14.19.1</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SCD4</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SCD5</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Stearoyl-CoA desaturase 2</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SCD2</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ACOD4</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Stearyl-CoA desaturase that utilizes O(2) and electronsfrom reduced cytochrome b5 to introduce the first double bond intosaturated fatty acyl-CoA substrates. Catalyzes the insertion of acis double bond at the delta-9 position into fatty acyl-CoAsubstrates including palmitoyl-CoA and stearoyl-CoA(PubMed:15907797, PubMed:15610069). Gives rise to a mixture of16:1 and 18:1 unsaturated fatty acids.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15610069, ECO:0000269|PubMed:15907797}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=2 [Fe(II)-cytochrome b5] + 2 H(+) + O2 + octadecanoyl-CoA= (9Z)-octadecenoyl-CoA + 2 [Fe(III)-cytochrome b5] + 2 H2O;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:19721, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:10438, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:10439, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:15379, ChEBI:CHEBI:29033, ChEBI:CHEBI:29034,ChEBI:CHEBI:57387, ChEBI:CHEBI:57394; EC=1.14.19.1;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:15610069,ECO:0000269|PubMed:15907797};COFACTOR:Name=Fe(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:29033;Evidence={ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P13516};Note=Expected to bind 2 Fe(2+) ions per subunit.{ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P13516};SUBUNIT: May self-associate and form homodimers.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15610069}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Endoplasmic reticulum membrane{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15907797}; Multi-pass membrane protein{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15907797}.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;Name=1;IsoId=Q86SK9-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=Q86SK9-2; Sequence=VSP_029883;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Detected in fetal brain, and at lower levelsin fetal kidney. Detected in adult brain and pancreas, and atlower levels in kidney and lung. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12727354,ECO:0000269|PubMed:15610069, ECO:0000269|PubMed:15907797}.DOMAIN: The histidine box domains are involved in binding thecatalytic metal ions. {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:O00767}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the fatty acid desaturase type 1 family.{ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference128966</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SCD5_HUMAN Reviewed; 330 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_79966</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_Q86SK9_identity</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

